WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.583 --> 00:00:02.335
Tonight, more classified documents.

00:00:02.335 --> 00:00:03.044
An outside

00:00:03.044 --> 00:00:04.504
team hired by lawyers

00:00:04.504 --> 00:00:06.131
for former President Trump

00:00:06.131 --> 00:00:08.174
finding two items marked classified

00:00:08.174 --> 00:00:09.467
in one of Trump's storage lockers

00:00:09.467 --> 00:00:10.719
in West Palm Beach.

00:00:10.719 --> 00:00:11.594
This all comes after

00:00:11.594 --> 00:00:11.928
the former

00:00:11.928 --> 00:00:13.763
president was directed by a federal judge

00:00:13.763 --> 00:00:14.764
to take a harder

00:00:14.764 --> 00:00:16.307
look at his properties for any remaining

00:00:16.307 --> 00:00:17.934
classified materials.

00:00:17.934 --> 00:00:19.477
So let's go straight to senior justice

00:00:19.477 --> 00:00:20.812
correspondent Evan Perez.

00:00:20.812 --> 00:00:21.312
I know, Evan,

00:00:21.312 --> 00:00:21.938
you've been speaking

00:00:21.938 --> 00:00:23.064
to your sources tonight.

00:00:23.064 --> 00:00:24.941
So let's just start off,

00:00:24.941 --> 00:00:25.608
first of all,

00:00:25.608 --> 00:00:27.610
with what more you've learned from them

00:00:27.610 --> 00:00:30.238
about these new classified documents.

00:00:30.655 --> 00:00:30.864
Well,

00:00:30.864 --> 00:00:32.115
these two documents were found

00:00:32.115 --> 00:00:35.452
in a storage unit in in Florida.

00:00:35.452 --> 00:00:37.328
This is one of the places that

00:00:37.328 --> 00:00:40.415
the Trump team had the items

00:00:40.415 --> 00:00:42.250
that were removed from the White House

00:00:42.250 --> 00:00:43.877
when he left office.

00:00:43.877 --> 00:00:45.170
The GSA had them

00:00:45.170 --> 00:00:46.546
transported down to Florida.

00:00:46.546 --> 00:00:47.589
And this is one of those places

00:00:47.589 --> 00:00:48.131
that they went.

00:00:48.131 --> 00:00:49.966
Now, Aaron, the importance of this

00:00:49.966 --> 00:00:52.093
is that obviously the former president

00:00:52.093 --> 00:00:55.138
and his team got a subpoena back in June,

00:00:55.138 --> 00:00:57.307
and they said that they had returned

00:00:57.307 --> 00:00:59.017
everything that was marked classified.

00:00:59.017 --> 00:01:00.018
This was what the subpoena

00:01:00.018 --> 00:01:02.437
demanded is a grand jury subpoena.

00:01:02.437 --> 00:01:04.355
Obviously, we know that that wasn't true

00:01:04.355 --> 00:01:05.899
because in August,

00:01:05.899 --> 00:01:07.108
the FBI did a search

00:01:07.108 --> 00:01:09.569
and found a lot more classified documents

00:01:10.028 --> 00:01:10.904
in their search.

00:01:10.904 --> 00:01:12.822
And since then, the Justice Department

00:01:12.822 --> 00:01:14.866
has been telling the Trump team

00:01:14.866 --> 00:01:15.325
that they believe

00:01:15.325 --> 00:01:16.618
that there were additional documents

00:01:16.618 --> 00:01:17.827
and their government records

00:01:17.827 --> 00:01:19.245
that were still missing.

00:01:19.245 --> 00:01:22.248
And that obviously he hadn't

00:01:22.248 --> 00:01:23.416
turned over everything.

00:01:23.416 --> 00:01:26.711
This is why the Trump team hired a team

00:01:26.920 --> 00:01:27.879
to do this

00:01:27.879 --> 00:01:29.255
search of four different properties,

00:01:29.255 --> 00:01:31.800
including Bedminster, the golf course,

00:01:31.800 --> 00:01:32.926
Trump Tower,

00:01:32.926 --> 00:01:33.885
this storage facility,

00:01:33.885 --> 00:01:35.470
and another office facility.

00:01:35.470 --> 00:01:37.722
So this is why the Trump

00:01:37.722 --> 00:01:39.099
team did this search.

00:01:39.099 --> 00:01:40.475
They invited the Justice Department

00:01:40.475 --> 00:01:41.935
to at least participate

00:01:41.935 --> 00:01:43.728
and the Justice Department declined.

00:01:43.728 --> 00:01:45.688
So now we'll see whether,

00:01:45.688 --> 00:01:46.147
you know,

00:01:46.147 --> 00:01:49.442
this satisfies the judge who has overseen

00:01:49.442 --> 00:01:51.194
all of this and has demanded that

00:01:51.194 --> 00:01:52.862
they turn over everything.

00:01:52.862 --> 00:01:54.322
All right, Evan, thank you very much.

00:01:54.322 --> 00:01:55.698
So let's go now to Ryan Goodman,

00:01:55.698 --> 00:01:56.741
the former special counsel

00:01:56.741 --> 00:01:57.700
at the Department of Defense.

00:01:57.700 --> 00:01:59.285
Now the coeditor in chief of the Just

00:01:59.285 --> 00:02:00.662
Security Legal Blog

00:02:00.662 --> 00:02:02.622
and a professor of law at NYU.

00:02:02.622 --> 00:02:02.956
All right.

00:02:02.956 --> 00:02:03.915
Every step of the way we've

00:02:03.915 --> 00:02:05.208
talked about this. And now

00:02:06.417 --> 00:02:07.752
what does this development mean?

00:02:07.752 --> 00:02:08.795
I mean, obviously, it means Mar

00:02:08.795 --> 00:02:09.838
a Lago is not the only place

00:02:09.838 --> 00:02:10.880
they were classified documents

00:02:10.880 --> 00:02:11.965
because these were in a storage

00:02:11.965 --> 00:02:13.049
locker in West Palm Beach.

00:02:13.049 --> 00:02:15.218
So it's a different location.

00:02:16.177 --> 00:02:18.054
And this outside team

00:02:18.054 --> 00:02:19.514
has found more classified documents.

00:02:19.514 --> 00:02:21.933
So what does it actually mean?

00:02:21.933 --> 00:02:24.227
So it doesn't necessarily mean

00:02:24.227 --> 00:02:25.395
that it's further evidence

00:02:25.395 --> 00:02:26.146
of the core

00:02:26.146 --> 00:02:27.355
crimes of willful

00:02:27.355 --> 00:02:29.607
retention of national defense information

00:02:29.983 --> 00:02:30.900
and concealment of government,

00:02:30.900 --> 00:02:31.985
because we already knew that

00:02:31.985 --> 00:02:32.527
that's already

00:02:32.527 --> 00:02:32.902
that's already

00:02:32.902 --> 00:02:33.945
there is an avalanche

00:02:33.945 --> 00:02:34.737
of information on that.

00:02:34.737 --> 00:02:36.906
All right. Okay.

00:02:36.906 --> 00:02:37.365
But it does

00:02:37.365 --> 00:02:39.409
go to the obstruction of justice

00:02:39.409 --> 00:02:41.744
and the disobeying of a subpoena.

00:02:42.245 --> 00:02:43.037
And it sounds like,

00:02:43.037 --> 00:02:44.289
according to a Washington Post

00:02:44.289 --> 00:02:46.082
reporting, that Judge Beryl,

00:02:46.082 --> 00:02:48.334
how is the fantastic judge in the D.C.

00:02:48.334 --> 00:02:50.545
Circuit said to them first?

00:02:50.545 --> 00:02:52.046
Again, a test to me

00:02:52.046 --> 00:02:53.214
that you have fully complied

00:02:53.214 --> 00:02:54.549
with the subpoena. They do so.

00:02:54.549 --> 00:02:55.925
And then

00:02:55.925 --> 00:02:57.427
they then she demands

00:02:57.427 --> 00:02:58.636
that they do this additional search.

00:02:58.636 --> 00:02:59.470
And lo and behold,

00:02:59.470 --> 00:03:01.055
it turns up more documents.

00:03:01.055 --> 00:03:01.389
And also,

00:03:01.389 --> 00:03:02.849
according to post reporting, it's

00:03:02.849 --> 00:03:04.267
not necessarily that they came straight

00:03:04.267 --> 00:03:04.893
from the White House,

00:03:04.893 --> 00:03:06.936
that they were potentially first

00:03:06.936 --> 00:03:09.189
at an office in North Virginia

00:03:09.480 --> 00:03:11.316
where Trump staffers were.

00:03:11.316 --> 00:03:13.693
And then the GSA only starts

00:03:13.693 --> 00:03:14.861
to rent out the facility

00:03:14.861 --> 00:03:16.279
in July of 20, 21.

00:03:16.279 --> 00:03:17.322
So that's already six months

00:03:17.322 --> 00:03:19.073
after he's left office. Right.

00:03:19.073 --> 00:03:20.074
So it's in North Virginia

00:03:20.074 --> 00:03:22.118
and then it's in parts of Florida.

00:03:22.118 --> 00:03:23.286
It's a real problem. Okay.

00:03:23.286 --> 00:03:24.037
So when you talk

00:03:24.037 --> 00:03:25.205
with the avalanche of information

00:03:25.205 --> 00:03:26.497
already in terms of,

00:03:26.497 --> 00:03:28.791
you know, well, for retention, have it.

00:03:28.791 --> 00:03:29.334
Okay.

00:03:29.334 --> 00:03:30.960
But now you're talking about this

00:03:30.960 --> 00:03:32.086
that maybe, maybe I don't know

00:03:32.086 --> 00:03:32.837
if I want to

00:03:32.837 --> 00:03:33.713
be putting words in your mouth,

00:03:33.713 --> 00:03:34.505
but maybe this moves

00:03:34.505 --> 00:03:36.382
the needle even more on obstruction

00:03:36.382 --> 00:03:37.342
So the reason for that

00:03:37.342 --> 00:03:38.551
may be that his lawyers

00:03:38.551 --> 00:03:40.511
reportedly did represent the Trump

00:03:40.511 --> 00:03:40.970
no longer

00:03:40.970 --> 00:03:43.389
had custody over any such records. Right.

00:03:43.389 --> 00:03:44.515
Since June.

00:03:44.515 --> 00:03:45.308
Now, obviously,

00:03:45.308 --> 00:03:46.976
the FBI search of Mar

00:03:46.976 --> 00:03:48.686
a Lago itself was post that point.

00:03:48.686 --> 00:03:50.438
But does this indicate

00:03:50.438 --> 00:03:52.357
that they directly lied?

00:03:52.357 --> 00:03:54.400
It is evidence that they were lying.

00:03:54.692 --> 00:03:56.027
It's not proof that they were lying.

00:03:56.027 --> 00:03:57.528
But part of what they say

00:03:57.528 --> 00:03:59.155
in writing to the Justice Department

00:03:59.155 --> 00:04:01.449
is that they attest at that time

00:04:01.824 --> 00:04:02.659
to the idea that they've done

00:04:02.659 --> 00:04:05.411
a diligent search of all boxes

00:04:05.411 --> 00:04:06.371
that went from the White House

00:04:06.371 --> 00:04:07.747
to Florida. Right.

00:04:07.747 --> 00:04:09.374
So they can't claim, oh,

00:04:09.374 --> 00:04:10.833
we just didn't know about this. Right.

00:04:10.833 --> 00:04:11.626
That's not an excuse.

00:04:11.626 --> 00:04:13.544
You have to know to certify.

00:04:13.544 --> 00:04:15.046
Exactly. Exactly.

00:04:15.046 --> 00:04:16.089
So it's not that they could say,

00:04:16.089 --> 00:04:16.756
oh, well,

00:04:16.756 --> 00:04:18.007
we didn't know that they were there.

00:04:18.007 --> 00:04:19.509
These two other documents.

00:04:19.509 --> 00:04:20.051
It's well,

00:04:20.051 --> 00:04:21.344
you told us that you did a diligent

00:04:21.344 --> 00:04:22.262
search

00:04:22.262 --> 00:04:23.805
of all the dark of all the boxes,

00:04:23.805 --> 00:04:24.639
and obviously you didn't,

00:04:24.639 --> 00:04:25.807
because when you got this outside firm,

00:04:25.807 --> 00:04:26.557
they found more.

00:04:26.557 --> 00:04:27.558
So what does this mean?

00:04:27.558 --> 00:04:28.476
I mean, you've been very clear.

00:04:28.476 --> 00:04:29.102
You've written

00:04:29.102 --> 00:04:30.395
more than a hundred page documents

00:04:30.395 --> 00:04:31.104
saying they have more

00:04:31.104 --> 00:04:32.146
than enough to charge in the Mar

00:04:32.146 --> 00:04:32.814
a Lago case.

00:04:32.814 --> 00:04:34.065
So does this change anything

00:04:34.065 --> 00:04:34.899
in terms of charges

00:04:34.899 --> 00:04:36.401
or possible penalties?

00:04:36.401 --> 00:04:38.194
I don't think it adds additional charges,

00:04:38.194 --> 00:04:38.945
but it certainly adds

00:04:38.945 --> 00:04:39.946
additional evidence.

00:04:39.946 --> 00:04:40.905
And not only that,

00:04:40.905 --> 00:04:42.156
but it's an aggravating factor.

00:04:42.156 --> 00:04:43.700
These are the kinds of factors

00:04:43.700 --> 00:04:44.534
the Justice Department

00:04:44.534 --> 00:04:46.119
routinely looks at to determine

00:04:46.119 --> 00:04:47.578
whether or not to indict.

00:04:47.578 --> 00:04:48.621
It is egregious

00:04:48.621 --> 00:04:50.707
that we're now to two years out

00:04:50.707 --> 00:04:51.833
from his presidency,

00:04:51.833 --> 00:04:54.043
and he still has even more documents

00:04:54.043 --> 00:04:55.712
after first giving false statements,

00:04:55.712 --> 00:04:56.879
second giving false statements.

00:04:56.879 --> 00:04:57.714
That's unaffected.

00:04:57.714 --> 00:04:58.631
That makes a difference. Right.

00:04:58.631 --> 00:04:59.340
It was interesting

00:04:59.340 --> 00:04:59.674
when you say,

00:04:59.674 --> 00:05:00.216
you know, intent

00:05:00.216 --> 00:05:01.384
may not matter to the facts

00:05:01.384 --> 00:05:02.010
of whether you have it,

00:05:02.010 --> 00:05:03.678
but when intent is so clear

00:05:03.678 --> 00:05:06.431
and so in your face, it means something.

00:05:06.556 --> 00:05:07.265
Yes. All right.

00:05:07.265 --> 00:05:08.725
Brian Goodwin, thank you very much.

